Algorithm:

1. Start the program.
2. Create a Binary Search Tree using nodes containing integer values.
3. Insert elements into the BST.
4. Display the original BST using inorder traversal.
5. Enter the value of the node to be deleted.
6. Search for the node in the BST.
7. Check whether the node has exactly one child.
8. If it has one child, connect its parent to that child and delete the node.
9. If the node does not have exactly one child or is not found, display an appropriate message.
10. Display the updated BST using inorder traversal.
11. Stop the program.
